<task id="130" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C8 — close the finance (and scorecard) recalculate IDOR and make the /api/finance gate authorize the record each route actually acts on (summary no longer always 403; no id-substitution on confirm/reject/search)</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C8)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs change on live, unconditionally mapped BFF routes (tags bff-api, auth, security); closes a cross-matter financial disclosure plus an app-only write.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security/auth-sensitive: one shared filter gates four finance routes with three different id kinds (route matter id, body document id, body matter/vendor ids, query ids), and each must authorize exactly the id its handler consumes — a per-route judgment, not a mechanical edit.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (GovernedFiles + census), which most register-driven auth tasks also touch, and Spaarke.Core OperationAccessPolicy.cs (completeness-tested shared registry).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-9 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Session 26 defect C8 (HIGH, 3/3 skeptics confirmed). Supersedes the summary half of finding A-20 that task 003 closed (task 003 fixed only the missing "finance.read" policy key; the matter id is still evaluated against sprk_documents). Scope widened at authoring (2026-09-30) by two leads the session-26 consolidator raised unverified and this author verified against source: ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints has the identical auth-only recalculate shape, and the finance filter's id-fallback chain lets confirm/reject/search authorize one id while acting on another.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Any signed-in user can POST /api/finance/{matters|projects}/{id}/recalculate (and /api/{matters|projects}/{id}/recalculate-grades) for a record they cannot see, and the BFF reads that record's invoices/budgets/KPIs app-only, overwrites its rollup fields app-only, and returns the numbers. Meanwhile GET /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/summary denies everyone because the matter id is checked as if it were a document. Make every one of these routes ask Dataverse, as the caller, about the exact record the handler touches — before any Dataverse read or write — and fail closed.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — BFF authorization filters and the Spaarke.Core caller-scoped access seam. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal API endpoint filters (ADR-008), ProblemDetails (ADR-019), and Dataverse RetrievePrincipalAccess over OBO. Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task: (1) the four recalculate routes (finance matter/project, scorecard matter/project) return the SAME 404 for an unknown id and for an id the caller cannot Read, before any Dataverse read or write, and a caller with Read gets 200 as today; (2) GET /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/summary evaluates the caller's rights on sprk_matters (not sprk_documents), so a caller with Read gets the summary and a caller without gets 403; (3) confirm, reject and invoice search each authorize exactly the id(s) their handler consumes — no route authorizes an id taken from a different source (query vs body) than the one it acts on; (4) FinanceEndpoints.cs, FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs and ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints.cs are classified in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests and pass Rule A/B; (5) the finance rollup/scorecard PATCH cannot create a record for a non-existent id; (6) the behaviour is proven live in dev with a non-admin test user.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 LIVE. Every anchor below verified against the working tree 2026-09-30.

RECALCULATE IDOR (untracked). `Api/Finance/FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs:28-31` and `:47-50` map the matter and project groups with only `.RequireRateLimiting("dataverse-query")` and a bare `.RequireAuthorization()`. There is no DefaultPolicy/FallbackPolicy in the BFF (`Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs:231` registers named policies only), so that means "authenticated". The shared handler `RecalculateAsync` (`:91-140`) calls the service with no record check. `Services/Finance/FinanceRollupService.cs:130-136` unwraps the APP-identity ServiceClient and queries sprk_invoice / sprk_budget app-only (`:236`, `:256`); `:189-193` PATCHes nine derived fields onto the parent through `IFieldMappingDataverseService.UpdateRecordFieldsAsync` (app-only `DataverseWebApiService.cs:1387-1410`, no If-Match); `:200-211` returns total spend, budget, utilization, velocity, average invoice and a 12-month timeline. Result: an authenticated user walled off from matter M learns M's finances and forces a write to M. Mapped unconditionally (`Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:361-362`; service registered unconditionally at `Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs:210`). The only tests (`tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/FinanceRollupEndpointsContractTests.cs:53-76`) assert the unauthenticated 401 and nothing else. Live caller: `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_subgrid_parent_rollup.js:452-467` acquires a delegated BFF token by MSAL SSO and treats any non-OK as a console warning (`:486`), so the status code chosen for a denial does not affect the form.

⚠️ `FinanceRollupService` is ALSO called app-only by `Services/Jobs/Handlers/SpendSnapshotGenerationJobHandler.cs:95`. The caller check therefore belongs at the ENDPOINT, never inside the service — putting it in the service breaks the background job (no caller token) or tempts an app-only fallback.

SAME SHAPE, SCORECARD (verified at authoring, was an unverified consolidator lead). `Api/ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints.cs:25-28` and `:43-46` — same groups, same bare `RequireAuthorization()`, same unguarded `RecalculateGradesAsync` (`:86-133`); `Services/ScorecardCalculatorService.cs:224` writes through the same app-only `UpdateRecordFieldsAsync`; mapped unconditionally at `Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:241`, service registered at `Program.cs:72`. `FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs:12` says it "Follows ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints pattern exactly" — the defect was copied. Fixing one and not the other leaves the same IDOR one URL over.
LIVE CALLERS OF recalculate-grades (reviewer-verified 2026-09-30) — three form web resources, all with a delegated MSAL token: `src/solutions/webresources/sprk_matter_kpi_refresh.js:276`, `sprk_kpi_subgrid_refresh.js:301`, and `sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js:270-353`. The last one RETRIES 3 times on any non-OK and then shows the user an alert "Unable to recalculate grades…" (`:366-372`), so a wrongly-denied honest user is VISIBLE there (unlike `sprk_subgrid_parent_rollup.js`, which only logs). `sprk_subgrid_parent_rollup.js:24` also defaults its template to `/api/{entityPath}/{entityId}/recalculate-grades`, so it can call either family.

SUMMARY ALWAYS 403 (mis-closed as A-20 by task 003). `Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs:16-19` attaches `AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter("finance.read")` to the whole `/api/finance` group, and `:64-65` again on the summary route. `Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:122-123` takes the route `matterId` as `ResourceId` and `:88` calls `AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync`, which resolves rights through `GetCallerAccessAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:76-80`, `:225`) → `DataverseAccessDataSource` whose RetrievePrincipalAccess target and fallback probe are hard-coded to `sprk_documents` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs:373`, `:662-663`, `:793`, `:812-818`). A matter id is never a document id → None → 403 for every honest caller. Task 003 (notes/task-003-operation-rights-decisions.md:88) marked the filter fixed after adding only the policy key. The entity-generic sibling already exists and is the fix: `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(userId, entitySetName, recordId, token)` (`AuthorizationService.cs:255-283`) → `DataverseAccessDataSource.GetRecordAccessAsync` (`:376-460`), OBO RetrievePrincipalAccess against the named entity set, Read-only probe fallback, None on every fault. Only known consumer of the summary route: the Copilot agent OpenAPI (`src/solutions/CopilotAgent/spaarke-bff-openapi.yaml:641`).

ID SUBSTITUTION ON THE OTHER THREE ROUTES (verified at authoring). The group-level filter runs on EVERY route in the group, and `ExtractResourceId` (`FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:116-147`) walks a fallback chain: route matterId → documentId → invoiceId → id → query matterId → documentId → invoiceId.
  • POST /invoice-review/confirm and /reject (`FinanceEndpoints.cs:22-47`) take their ids from the JSON BODY (`InvoiceReviewConfirmRequest.DocumentId/MatterId/VendorOrgId`, DTO at `Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs:54-76`; handlers `FinanceEndpoints.cs:84-130` and `:136-181`, validated `:186-221`). The filter never reads the body: a body-only request gets 400 "Resource identifier not found", and a request that adds `?documentId=&lt;a document I can write&gt;` passes both filters while the handler confirms/rejects the BODY's document and links a new sprk_invoice to the BODY's matter — authorize one id, act on another.
  • GET /invoices/search (`:50-61`, handler `:227-312`) binds an OPTIONAL `matterId` query. `?documentId=&lt;my document&gt;` with no matterId passes the filter, and `Services/Finance/InvoiceSearchService.cs:171-180` then builds a tenant-only filter — a tenant-wide invoice search.
No src client calls confirm/reject/search today (grep of src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js} for "invoice-review" and "invoices/search": 0 hits), so tightening them breaks no shipped caller.

GUARD GAP. `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:99-101` — everything not in `GovernedFiles` (`:126-`) is NotGoverned; Api/Finance/* and Api/ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints.cs are absent, which is how an auth-only write route stayed invisible.

REUSE, NOT NEW MACHINERY. Two existing caller-rights mechanisms already answer "what may THIS caller do to record X of entity set S":
  • `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` (above) — used by `Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs:497-516`: `GetCallerRecordAccessAsync(callerOid, entitySetName, parentId, callerToken)` then `snapshot.AccessRights.HasFlag(Read)`, with a uniform deny. Goes through `CachedAccessDataSource` (see notes re C12).
  • `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync(token, entitySet, recordId, ct)` (`Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:68-`, OBO WhoAmI + RetrievePrincipalAccess, no read-probe fallback, None on every fault) — used by `Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:79-232`, which is ALREADY a route-value → caller-rights → `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights` → fail-closed endpoint filter (attached at `Api/OBOEndpoints.cs:180`, `:425`). Its route keys are fixed to `{entityLogicalName}`/`{recordId}` (`:104-108`) and it denies 403, so it does not fit the finance routes as-is — but it is the nearest existing shape and the first candidate to EXTEND (parameterize route key, fixed entity type, deny status) before adding anything.
Note the probe carries a ~1.6 s not-found backoff (`CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs:99-104`) that also lands on genuine denials; on the recalculate routes that delay is invisible to `sprk_subgrid_parent_rollup.js` but lengthens the quick-create retry loop above.
ENTITY-SET NAMES. Two logical-name → entity-set maps already exist and EACH declares itself the only one: `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:98-148`, exposed via `TryResolveEntitySet` `:167-178`; remarks at `:101-106` say a fourth map "is a review failure"; LOCKSTEP invariant with `DocumentAssociationMap` at `:111-116`) and `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` (`:135-155`). Both contain sprk_matter→sprk_matters and sprk_project→sprk_projects; NEITHER contains the vendor organization. The finance routes' entity types are FIXED by the route, not taken from request input, so a per-route constant set name (the `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:80` `ProjectEntitySet = "sprk_projects"` precedent) or a `TryResolveEntitySet` call satisfies "never pluralize" without a new map. The vendor lookup `sprk_invoice.sprk_vendororg` targets `sprk_organization` (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateInvoiceWizard/invoiceService.ts:15`, `:220`); its entity SET name must be read from live metadata, not guessed.
`OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights(rights, operation)` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs:293`) maps an operation key to required rights; "finance.read" → Read (`:165-167`), "finance.confirm" → Write (`:169-174`, whose comment records a prior decision NOT to require Create for the sprk_invoice that confirm creates), "entity.associate_document" → AppendTo (`:176-186`). The `:165-166` comment ("Resource = matter / document / invoice id") describes the id-fallback chain this task deletes and must be corrected.</background>
