  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every route touched. Fail closed. A missing caller oid, a missing bearer token, an unresolvable Dataverse user, a RetrievePrincipalAccess fault, or any exception in the check DENIES. There is no app-only fallback on any path — `GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` already refuses without a token; do not add a branch around it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the four recalculate routes (finance matters/projects, scorecard matters/projects). The caller check runs BEFORE any Dataverse read or write, as an ENDPOINT FILTER in each route's own fluent chain (ADR-008; and so RouteAuthorizationGuardTests Rule A can see it — a handler-internal check would force the file into the HandlerAuthorized scope, where Rule A does not apply and the guard proves nothing) — NEVER inside FinanceRollupService or ScorecardCalculatorService, which SpendSnapshotGenerationJobHandler calls app-only. Required right on the parent record = Read (decided at authoring: the response discloses only values that the parent's own rollup columns expose to any reader of the parent after the write, and the write is deterministic server-derived data, so Read is the boundary that closes the disclosure without denying the form users who trigger the rollup).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: recalculate denial shape. An id the caller cannot Read and an id that does not exist return the IDENTICAL response: 404, same title, same detail text, same reasonCode, same extension keys. A 403 for "exists but denied" would be an existence oracle. Do not echo whether the record exists anywhere in the body or logs returned to the caller. The handlers' existing `KeyNotFoundException` 404s (`FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs:118-126`, `ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints.cs:112-120`), which today put the id and a per-entity title in the body, adopt the SAME uniform shape, so a record deleted between check and compute is indistinguishable too.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: /api/finance routes. Each route authorizes exactly the id(s) its handler consumes, taken from the SAME source the handler binds (route value for summary; request BODY for confirm/reject; the query `matterId` for search). Delete the cross-kind fallback chain in `ExtractResourceId`: no route may authorize a documentId when it acts on a matterId, or a query id when it acts on a body id. Rules per route: summary → Read on sprk_matters(matterId); search → `matterId` REQUIRED (400 when absent) and Read on sprk_matters(matterId); reject → Write on the body DocumentId via the existing document path (`AuthorizeAsync`, "finance.confirm"); confirm → Write on the body DocumentId AND AppendTo on EVERY record the handler writes into a lookup of the new sprk_invoice — all three: DocumentId (sprk_invoice.sprk_document; Write does not imply AppendTo in Dataverse), MatterId → sprk_matters (sprk_invoice.sprk_matter), VendorOrgId → the sprk_organization entity set (sprk_invoice.sprk_vendororg; `InvoiceReviewService.cs:148-150`, `:261-263`) — AppendTo because that is the right Dataverse itself demands to attach a record to a parent (same reasoning as "entity.associate_document", `OperationAccessPolicy.cs:176-186`). A body id that is `Guid.Empty` or missing is a 400 (the existing field-level validation, `FinanceEndpoints.cs:186-221`) returned BEFORE any Dataverse call — do not spend a rights query on an empty id, and do not let the filter's ordering turn a validation error into a 403.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the group-level filter at `FinanceEndpoints.cs:18`. Remove it and gate each of the four routes explicitly, so every route's authorization is visible in its own fluent chain (Rule A) and no route is double-gated with a filter that cannot find its id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: entity-set names. Never derive by pluralizing a logical name; a wrong set name fails closed as a 404/403 indistinguishable from "denied", which hides the bug. Every route here has a FIXED entity type, so use a per-route constant or `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet` (matter/project) — do NOT declare a new logical-name → entity-set map (`EntityAccessFilter.cs:101-106`), and do NOT add `sprk_organization` (or anything else) to `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (lockstep invariant with `DocumentAssociationMap`, `:111-116`) or to `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` (widens what `POST /api/ai/search` accepts). The sprk_organization set name is read from live `EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_organization')?$select=EntitySetName` and recorded in the task note before it is written into code; each constant set name is pinned by a test that names the live-verified value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every deny added. Carry a machine-readable reasonCode (e.g. `sdap.access.deny.*` convention) in ProblemDetails (ADR-019). For the recalculate 404 the reasonCode is the same for absent and denied.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the rollup/scorecard PATCH. The write must not create a record for an id that does not exist. The pre-check already stops the ordinary case; verify live whether a Dataverse Web API PATCH without If-Match on a deleted/non-existent id upserts, and if it does, close the check-then-write race on THESE two write paths only (e.g. an If-Match: * on the rollup/scorecard writes) without changing behaviour for other `UpdateRecordFieldsAsync` callers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: `InvoiceReviewService.CreateInvoiceRecordAsync` (`Services/Finance/InvoiceReviewService.cs:254-300`). It CREATES the invoice by an If-Match-less PATCH on a new GUID (`:294-299`, "upsert pattern") — so the no-upsert guarantee above must NOT be applied to `UpdateRecordFieldsAsync` globally. It also writes its three lookups as `_{lookup}_value` keys (`:260-263`), which the Dataverse Web API does not accept as a lookup write (lookups are written with `{NavigationProperty}@odata.bind`). Today confirm is unreachable (every body-only request 400s at the filter), so this has never run; this task makes it reachable. Verify it live as part of the gate; if the create fails or silently drops the lookups, fix the lookup writes here using navigation-property names read from live metadata (verified by read-back, as `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.AssignOwnerToSecureTeamAsync` does for ownerid), because shipping a newly reachable route that 500s is not a fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute at the IAccessDataSource / AuthorizationService boundary (the existing contract-test fixture pattern at `FinanceRollupEndpointsContractTests.cs:85-150` hosts the REAL `Map*Endpoints` in-process). No live Dataverse in CI — live proof is the manual gate below.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF — these are existing BFF routes; no new service) citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master from a short path, both sides zipped with Compress-Archive, file counts equal; report both absolute sizes and the delta; ceiling 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — no new HIGH.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: new surface. No new filter class: extend `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` (body/query ids on /api/finance) and, for the fixed-type route-id checks, either the same filter or `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` (parameterized route key / fixed entity type / deny status) — whichever the executor extends, the other is not duplicated. Any new type or OperationAccessPolicy key must carry the three-question justification in the PR, with grep evidence. Whichever filter is used must stay credited by `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.FilterMarker` (`:1880-1884`) AND inspected by Rule B (`:1088-`) — a renamed or new filter name that Rule A credits but Rule B never inspects is the SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter defect (`:1862-1867`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (binding)">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred; scope discovered during execution is added to this task, not pushed off. No Dataverse test in CI; the live check is a MANUAL gate using the existing non-admin test users in their current business unit — do not relocate users.</constraint>
  </constraints>

