  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Re-verify every anchor in the background against current source (line numbers drift); in particular read `InvoiceReviewService.ConfirmInvoiceAsync` to enumerate exactly which request ids it writes into lookups, and `ScorecardCalculatorService` to confirm its reads are app-only.</step>
    <step order="1">Rework `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` so each route declares which id it authorizes, from which source (route/body/query), against which entity set, for which operation — and route matter/project ids through `GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` + `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights`, document ids through the existing document path. Delete the fallback chain.</step>
    <step order="2">Re-wire FinanceEndpoints.cs: drop the group-level filter; gate summary, search, confirm, reject per the route rules in the constraints; make search's matterId required.</step>
    <step order="3">Gate the four recalculate routes (finance + scorecard) with the same mechanism, returning the uniform 404 for unreadable-or-absent before any service call.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify live (read-only on a throwaway id first, then as part of the manual gate) whether an If-Match-less PATCH upserts; if it does, apply the no-upsert guarantee to the two rollup write paths only.</step>
    <step order="5">Add GovernedFiles entries for Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs, Api/Finance/FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs and Api/ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints.cs with Scope = RouteLevelGate and a reason; confirm Rule A, Rule B and the census pass; perturbation-prove it (remove one route's filter locally, confirm Rule A FAILS naming that route, restore — the practice at `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:517-518`, `:538-539`) and record the result in the task note; register any new operation key and keep OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests green; correct the stale "finance.read" comment at `OperationAccessPolicy.cs:165-166`.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests (see acceptance criteria for the closed set of behaviours).</step>
    <step order="7">Build, unit + integration + arch suites, publish-size and CVE checks per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
    <step order="8">Run the manual live gate in dev and record the results (ids redacted to first 8 chars) in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-130-finance-authorization.md, including the task-003 supersession note.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A shipped consumer (in or outside src — ask if the Copilot agent or a Power Automate flow calls it) depends on UNSCOPED invoice search (no matterId). Requiring matterId is the fail-closed default; a tenant-wide search would need per-result trimming, which is a design decision — STOP and present options per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than re-allowing an unscoped search.</trigger>
    <trigger>The live gate shows a user who legitimately triggers the subgrid rollup (edits invoices/budgets on a matter they can open) is denied by the Read rule on the parent — that means the required right is wrong for a real population; STOP and report rather than widening to app-only or dropping the check.</trigger>
    <trigger>`InvoiceReviewService` writes a caller-supplied id into a field that is NOT a lookup (so AppendTo is not the obvious right), or writes to a record type outside the finance domain: STOP and name the field and the proposed right before choosing.</trigger>
    <trigger>The implementation appears to need a NEW logical-name → entity-set map, or an entry added to `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` or `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` (both are shared, and the first carries a lockstep invariant with DocumentAssociationMap): STOP and bring the choice to the owner rather than silently widening a different surface. The route-fixed constant (constraint above) is the recommended path and should make this trigger unnecessary.</trigger>
    <trigger>PRIVILEGE QUESTION ON CONFIRM (surfaced by the reviewer, not decided here). Confirm creates an `sprk_invoice` APP-ONLY (`InvoiceReviewService.cs:294-300`), so the caller's own Create privilege on sprk_invoice is never consulted; `OperationAccessPolicy.cs:171-173` records a prior decision not to require Create — but that note is about Create on the DOCUMENT, not the invoice table. If the live gate shows a user who can Write the document and AppendTo the matter/vendor but whose role lacks Create on sprk_invoice (check the test users' roles), STOP and present per CLAUDE.md §6: (a) RECOMMENDED — perform the sprk_invoice create under the caller's OBO token (not impersonation), so Dataverse enforces Create + AppendTo natively and the pre-checks become confirmatory; (b) keep app-only creation and record the decision in the ADR-tensions of this task's PR. Do not silently ship either.</trigger>
    <trigger>The live gate shows a user who legitimately saves a KPI assessment on a matter/project they can open gets the `sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js` "Unable to recalculate grades" alert after this change: STOP and report (same reasoning as the rollup trigger above) — do not widen to app-only.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:40-148` (the finance gate being reworked); `AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:255-283`, consumers at `Api/Filters/SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.cs:497`, `Api/Filters/ContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter.cs:299`, `Api/Ai/RecordSearchEndpoints.cs:284`, `Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs:765`, `Api/Ai/SemanticSearchEndpoints.cs:569`); entity-set maps `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (`Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:108-148`, via `TryResolveEntitySet` `:167-178`) and `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` (`:144-155`). A route-id → caller-rights endpoint filter ALREADY EXISTS: `Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:79-232` (task 076; `CallerRecordAccessProbe` + `OperationAccessPolicy.HasRequiredRights`, fail closed, attached at `Api/OBOEndpoints.cs:180`, `:425`) — reviewer correction 2026-09-30: the authoring note said a grep found none. It reads the fixed route keys `{entityLogicalName}`/`{recordId}` and denies 403, so it does not fit the finance routes unmodified.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — no new filter class and no new service. Extend `FinanceAuthorizationFilter` to take a per-route resource declaration (source route/body/query, entity set, operation) for the /api/finance routes; for the four fixed-type recalculate routes extend either that filter or `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` (route-key + fixed-entity + deny-status parameters), and do not do both. The only possible new surface is an OperationAccessPolicy key (e.g. for recalculate = Read) if an existing key's name would misdescribe the operation; reuse "finance.read" / "entity.associate_document" semantics where they fit.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any authenticated user reads a walled-off matter's or project's spend, budget, utilization and 12-month timeline and forces an app-only write to it (recalculate + recalculate-grades); the finance summary returns 403 to every caller; confirm/reject/search accept `?documentId=` for one record while acting on another (including a tenant-wide invoice search).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs</output>
