  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Recalculate (each of: finance matters, finance projects, scorecard matters, scorecard projects): given a caller whose rights on the parent are None, the response is 404 AND neither the rollup/scorecard service nor any Dataverse read/write is invoked (asserted on the substituted seams).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Recalculate: the response for a non-existent id, for an existing-but-unreadable id, and for a `KeyNotFoundException` raised by the service after the check passed are byte-identical apart from correlation/trace ids (status, title, detail, reasonCode, extension keys); none of them contains the requested id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Recalculate: given a caller with Read on the parent, the route returns 200 with the recalculated payload (behaviour unchanged for authorized callers).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Recalculate: with no bearer token forwarded (authenticated principal but token unreadable) or with the access seam throwing, the route denies (404 per the uniform shape) — no app-only path is taken.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Recalculate: unauthenticated requests still return 401 (existing tests stay green).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SpendSnapshotGenerationJobHandler still calls FinanceRollupService with no caller context and is unaffected (no code path in the service consults a caller).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Summary: a caller with Read on sprk_matters(matterId) gets 200 (or the existing 404 "no financial data" when the service returns null); a caller with None gets 403 with a reasonCode; the rights query targets the sprk_matters entity set, never sprk_documents (asserted on the entity-set argument reaching the seam).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Search: a request without matterId gets 400; a request with a matterId the caller cannot Read gets 403; `?documentId=` or `?invoiceId=` alone no longer authorizes anything (400); with a readable matterId the search runs scoped to that matter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Confirm: a body DocumentId the caller cannot Write → 403; each of DocumentId, MatterId and VendorOrgId the caller lacks AppendTo on → 403 (three separate cases, each asserting the rights query named that id AND the expected entity set — sprk_documents / sprk_matters / the live-verified sprk_organization set); on every 403 the invoice-review service is not invoked; a query-string documentId that differs from the body DocumentId has no effect on the decision (the body id is the one authorized); body-only requests from an authorized caller no longer 400 at the filter; a body with an empty DocumentId/MatterId/VendorOrgId gets the field-level 400 and no rights query is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reject: the body DocumentId is authorized at Write; a query-string id cannot substitute for it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Confirm, authorized caller: the created sprk_invoice carries the document, matter and vendor-organization lookups (proven live in gate item (f); if the lookup writes had to be changed, a test pins the payload uses `@odata.bind` and never `_{lookup}_value` keys).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The four /api/finance routes each carry their own authorization filter in the fluent chain; the group-level "finance.read" filter is gone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests: FinanceEndpoints.cs, FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs and ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints.cs are in GovernedFiles with Scope = RouteLevelGate and a reason; Rule A, Rule B and the census tests pass; no waiver is added for any of the EIGHT routes in these three files (4 in FinanceEndpoints, 2 in FinanceRollupEndpoints, 2 in ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints); the task note records the perturbation proof (a removed filter makes Rule A fail naming that route).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Filter reach (so an attached filter cannot be decorative): for each of the eight routes, a test through the REAL `Map*Endpoints` host shows that a caller the seam reports as None is denied on that route — a test that invokes the filter class directly, or only asserts a mock was called, does not satisfy this criterion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new logical-name → entity-set map exists, and `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` / `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` are unchanged (diff shows no entries added); the sprk_organization set name used in code equals the live-metadata value recorded in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests pass, including any operation key this task adds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If live verification shows an If-Match-less PATCH upserts: the rollup and scorecard writes carry a no-create guarantee and a test pins it; if it does not upsert, the live evidence is recorded in the task note and no write-path change is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover exactly the behaviours listed above plus the fail-closed branches named in the constraints. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build green; unit, integration and NetArchTest suites green; publish size reported against a fresh origin/master build per CLAUDE.md §10 (both absolute sizes, delta, zip tool, equal file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, existing non-admin test users in their current BU): (a) a user with NO access to matter M → POST /api/finance/matters/{M}/recalculate and POST /api/matters/{M}/recalculate-grades return 404 and M's modifiedon is unchanged; (b) a user with Read on M → both return 200; (c) POST recalculate on a random GUID returns 404 and no sprk_matter/sprk_project row with that id exists afterwards; (d) GET /api/finance/matters/{M}/summary returns 200 (or the documented 404 "no financial data") for the reader and 403 for the non-reader; (e) the subgrid rollup on the matter form still refreshes for the reader, and saving a KPI assessment from the quick-create form on a matter the reader can open updates grades WITHOUT the "Unable to recalculate grades" alert (`sprk_kpiassessment_quickcreate.js:366-372`); (f) a user with Write on a classified document and AppendTo on it, its matter and its vendor organization confirms it as an invoice and the new sprk_invoice row carries all three lookups (read back), while a user lacking AppendTo on the matter gets 403, no sprk_invoice row is created and the document's sprk_invoicereviewstatus is unchanged; (g) the test users' security roles' Create privilege on sprk_invoice is recorded (input to the confirm privilege escalation trigger). Results recorded in notes/task-130-finance-authorization.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Defect C8 — projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md § "[HIGH] C8" (evidence, tracking, fix direction) and the consolidator's "New leads" list (the scorecard and filter id-substitution leads are verified above and folded in; the upsert lead is closed by constraint + live check). Owner directives: notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md (round 2 is binding — no deferral, manual live gate). Supersedes the summary half of A-20 claimed fixed by task 003; code-quality-and-assurance-r3 task 023 only removed AllowAnonymous from the recalculate routes. Caching: `CachedAccessDataSource.GetRecordAccessAsync` (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Caching/CachedAccessDataSource.cs:145-213`) already keys record snapshots in a separate "record" namespace that includes the entity set, so moving the matter id off the document path cannot collide with document snapshots. Related but NOT in this task: C12 (CachedAccessDataSource caches None snapshots for 60 s, so a newly-granted reader may see the 404 for up to a minute — owned by task 132). If the executor extends `RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` / `CallerRecordAccessProbe` instead, that path is uncached, so C12 does not apply to it. Reviewer amendments 2026-09-30 (adversarial review, finance-provisioning group): corrected the §11 "existing" claim (RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter exists), replaced the SemanticSearch allow-list as "the map" with the route-fixed-constant rule (EntityAccessFilter's map has a lockstep invariant; neither map holds sprk_organization), named the three recalculate-grades web-resource callers and the quick-create alert, made AppendTo cover all three confirm lookups, fixed the route count (eight, not nine), required RouteLevelGate + a perturbation proof + a real-host filter-reach test, and surfaced the sprk_invoice Create-privilege question as an escalation trigger.</notes>

